.TH zlogin "" "Administration"
.SH NAME
zlogin \- graphical login on the hi-res console
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fB/etc/zlogin\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
.HS
zlogin -- graphical login on the hi-res console
Usage:	/etc/zlogin
Spawned by /etc/getty on the hi-res console in place of the textual
login prompt.  Draws a login panel on the bitmap display, checks the
name and password against /etc/passwd, and starts the zview desktop
as the session.
.HE
.B zlogin
is the graphical front door of the hi-res machine.
When
.B getty
finds itself on the hi-res console (the console driver reports the
.B vt100
terminal type and the video card answers a memory probe), it replaces
itself with
.B zlogin
instead of printing the textual login prompt.
.B zlogin
paints a login panel directly on the bitmap display and reads the
keyboard from the console in raw mode; no window server is running
yet, and the mouse is not used.
.PP
The panel holds a name field and a password field.
Printable characters go to the field that holds the caret;
the following keys edit and move:
.DS
.ta 16n
\fBEnter\fR	move from the name to the password field, or log in
\fBTab\fR	switch fields
\fBBackspace\fR	erase the last character
\fBCtrl-U\fR	clear the field
.DE
The password is shown as
.B *
characters.
.PP
The name and password are checked against
.B /etc/passwd
by the same rules as
.BR login :
an account whose password field is empty needs no password.
A successful login is recorded in
.B /etc/utmp
and
.BR /usr/adm/wtmp ,
the console is given to the user, the
.BR HOME ,
.B PATH
and
.B TERM
environment is set up, and
.B zlogin
replaces itself with
.BR /usr/hr/bin/zview ,
the desktop, running as the logged-in user.
When the desktop is quit,
.B init
starts
.B getty
on the console again and the login panel returns.
A failed attempt prints
.B Login incorrect
on the panel and is recorded in
.BR /usr/adm/failed .
.PP
If the video card is absent or the panel font cannot be read,
.B zlogin
gives the console back to the textual prompt: it replaces itself with
.B /etc/getty
passing the extra argument
.BR text ,
which tells
.B getty
not to try the graphical path again.
.SH FILES
.DS
.ta 28n
\fB/etc/passwd\fR	accounts and passwords
\fB/usr/hr/fonts/gacha.b.hf\fR	the panel font
\fB/usr/hr/bin/zview\fR	the session started on success
\fB/etc/utmp\fR	who is logged in
\fB/usr/adm/wtmp\fR	login accounting
\fB/usr/adm/failed\fR	failed attempts
.DE
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR getty ,
.BR init ,
.BR login ,
.B zview
.SH NOTES
.B zlogin
is started by
.B getty
and is not ordinarily run by hand: it draws over the whole display and
takes the console keyboard into raw mode.
.PP
The desktop's driver loading is restricted to the superuser, so at
present only a root login reaches the desktop; another account is
authenticated but its session exits at once and the login panel
returns.
